## B. Finding (1) — empty text reported as success: CONFIRMED, FIXED
Code on main: Gateway.complete/_run_stream returned ok=True with parsed["text"] == "" when the provider answered 200 with no
content (a thinking model that spent max_tokens before writing).
Live reproduction on main (real model, section D): {"ok":true,"reason":"ok","finish_reason":"length","tokens_in":33,"tokens_out":8}
and the stream: events ["route"], reason "ok".
Fix (D-162): no text (blank counts) AND no tool call -> ok=False, reason=empty_output, text=None; route, key source, finish_reason,
tokens, cost, provider_request_id kept (it was billed); not retried, no fallback (one call = one bill line). Same in complete and
stream, both adapters. A tool call with no text stays ok; text cut by the limit stays ok.

## C. Finding (3) — unknown model named platform_key_not_allowed: CONFIRMED, FIXED
platform_policy_from_env("free") returned catalog.is_free(...) -> False for an unknown model -> "platform_key_not_allowed".
Fix: Catalog.has_model (True/False when a loaded catalog can say, None otherwise); the free policy returns "model_not_found"
for a model a loaded catalog does not list; Gateway._credential accepts True (allow) or a known reason string; anything else ->
platform_key_not_allowed. Catalog not loaded / other provider -> unknown -> platform_key_not_allowed (no guess).
The user's own key is not judged by the catalog (the provider answers: 404 -> model_or_endpoint_not_found).
scripts/v2/r206_live_check.py now expects reason == model_not_found for the unknown-model check.

## D. Finding (2) — deleting a workspace deletes its call log: CONFIRMED (prod FK = CASCADE), NOT CHANGED (owner decision)
006 says so on purpose ("workspace deleted -> its calls go"), and D-155 says a deleted user leaves nothing behind.
Options for the owner (none applied; no migration written):
  A. keep CASCADE (today): most private; the operator loses cost/usage history of a deleted workspace; once R-207 counts
     platform usage from model_calls, delete+recreate a workspace would reset the count (quota bypass).
  B. migration 007: workspace_id nullable + ON DELETE SET NULL; rows of a deleted workspace become invisible to every user
     (RLS is_member(NULL) is false) and stay for the operator (service_role) as metadata only; user deletion still CASCADEs
     (D-155 kept). Rollback: back to CASCADE after deleting orphan rows. Needs a tested 007 + rollback + owner approval to apply.
  C. soft-delete workspaces (deleted_at) — wider change across 001/002 and every RLS policy; not recommended now.
Recommendation: B, decided together with R-207's quota design; until then A stays and is documented.

